LINPACK — Public-Domain Notice and Provenance

Source:
https://www.netlib.org/linpack/

LINPACK is a collection of Fortran subroutines for solving linear
equations, linear least-squares problems, and related matrix
factorization problems.

The LINPACK software distributed by Netlib is described in Netlib
and associated publications as public-domain software.

This file is a provenance notice for the LINPACK routines included
with this project; it is not a newly imposed license on LINPACK.

Original LINPACK source comments, authorship information, and
attribution should be retained when redistributing the routines.

Principal authors:
J. J. Dongarra
C. B. Moler
J. R. Bunch
G. W. Stewart

References confirming public-domain status include Netlib publications
that describe LINPACK, EISPACK, and LAPACK as public-domain linear
algebra libraries.

https://www.netlib.org/lapack/lawnspdf/lawn58.pdf


